.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="In a TPD experiment a covered surface is heated at a steady rate \beta while the desorbing gas is recorded, and each binding state shows up as a peak. simulate_tpd integrates the Polanyi-Wigner rate equation to produce these spectra. Redhead (1962) turned a first-order peak temperature T_p into a desorption energy: E_d = RT_p[\ln(\nu T_p/\beta) - 3.64] (~chemistrykit.surface.systems.tpd.redhead_desorption_energy). Below, the formula is checked against the exact peak condition (~chemistrykit.surface.systems.tpd.first_order_peak_temperature). First-order peaks shift with heating rate but not with coverage, while second-order peaks move to lower temperature as the coverage rises.">

